       "text": "I can't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and the order would give 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. I'm not able to enter a dose above that limit based on a confirmation alone.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum, and I can add a note such as \"give with food.\"\n- **Enter another regimen within the limit.** Examples are 600 mg four times daily or 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you believe the patient needs more than the labeled maximum, you can ask pharmacy or the attending to review it. They can go through the institution's process for an off-label dose. Another option is to consider a different or additional analgesic strategy.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
